WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.088
Replaying the examples
turns up some real traps.

2
00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:06.418
The list examples show
one page for one person,

3
00:00:06.418 --> 00:00:09.399
but a busy subscription spans many pages.

4
00:00:09.399 --> 00:00:12.689
One example's role ID and
its friendly name disagree,

5
00:00:12.689 --> 00:00:16.437
so code that trusts the name
files a row under the wrong role.

6
00:00:16.437 --> 00:00:20.405
Another example says "assigned",
but it's really an activation,

7
00:00:20.405 --> 00:00:23.500
and read naively it looks
like standing access.

8
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.188
The scope is written three different
ways, which quietly breaks any diff.

9
00:00:28.188 --> 00:00:30.922
And the sample eligibility lasts a year,

10
00:00:30.922 --> 00:00:34.401
with no justification,
longer than any tier allows.

11
00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:36.580
Each of these is pinned by a test.
